<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swahili</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Swahili merchants</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swahili are a people of the East African coast, whose culture developed through interaction between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> Africans and Arab and Persian traders. Swahili merchants traded gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and other goods. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> profiles describe their role in trade with the interior.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swahili.jpg" alt="Swahili" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ji-Elle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuscrit_colonial_kiswahili-Africa_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
